# Direct dependencies for pass-secret-service, the headless D-Bus Secret
# Service backend this action installs so tests exercising the
# libsecret/keychain code path have something to talk to on Linux CI runners.
#
# CSO-CICD-01: this pip install used to run unpinned, in the same job as
# RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY (publish-on-tag.yml). Hash-pinning every package, direct
# and transitive (via --generate-hashes in requirements.txt), means a
# compromised or typosquatted release on PyPI cannot install silently even if
# a maintainer bumps a version here without re-auditing it: the installed
# bytes must match a hash captured at pin time. The signing key is also now
# scoped out of this job entirely (see publish-on-tag.yml), so this pin is
# defense in depth, not the only control.
#
# Regeneration command (matches the Concordia sidecar convention in
# sidecars/concordia/requirements.in; needs the system build deps this
# action's own "Install libsecret and pass-secret-service prerequisites" step
# installs, since pygobject/pycairo build from source):
#   python3.12 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install pip-tools
#   .venv/bin/pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file requirements.txt requirements.in
pygobject<3.50
cryptography
pass-secret-service
